**FRAMEWORK GUIDANCE (AUTO):**
- Overview: Auto-detected framework. Using adaptive selectors based on DOM patterns.
- Selector Tips: Prefer semantic selectors (getByRole, getByLabel, getByText) that work across all frameworks.
- Component Patterns: Look for common patterns: buttons (role="button"), forms (role="form"), inputs (role="textbox"), links (role="link").
- Wait Strategies: Use waitForLoadState("domcontentloaded") for initial loads; waitForSelector for dynamic elements.
- Form Interaction: Use getByLabel for inputs, getByRole for buttons and selects.
- Modal Handling: Wait for modal visibility before interaction: await page.locator(".modal").waitFor({ state: "visible" });
- Dynamic Content: For dynamic content, use waitForSelector with timeout or waitForLoadState.

**CODE EXAMPLES:**
// Generic button click
await page.getByRole('button', { name: /submit|save|send/i }).click();

// Generic form fill
await page.getByLabel('Email').fill('user@example.com');
await page.getByLabel('Password').fill('password123');

**COMMON PITFALLS:** Avoid framework-specific class names; use accessible roles and labels instead.

